      "evidence": "no licence has been activated from this project and nothing has been executed, so no qualification record exists. The SDK's own ReadMe defines installation as extracting the archive and then activating the licensing software, and the second step starts a 30-day trial bound to one machine — a decision that belongs to the maintainer rather than to a preflight (spec section 32). The artifact is present and verified, and the documentation describes the intended behaviour, but a documented intention is not a measurement: this gate is about what a running licensed engine does.",
      "gate": "EXTRACTION_PROFILE",
      "how_this_would_be_lifted": "The maintainer activates the 30-day trial on one chosen platform — the vendor's documented route is Trial = true in the licensing configuration and starting the licensing service, with no serial number and no personal information — runs the bounded qualification harness on fixtures that are not SD300, and re-runs this stage. No licence is bypassed, no trial is reset and no protection mechanism is touched (spec section 32).",
      "why_this_blocks_algorithm_4": "Each of these changes the template, and therefore the score. The pinned manual gives every one of them a type and a meaning and states a default for none of them — while it does state defaults for the face-side settings in the same tables, so the absence is a property of the document rather than of the reading. A value nobody recorded still decides the score, and a profile with 7 unrecorded values is not frozen. What is settled is the inventory itself and the 1 setting whose value upstream's own 1:1 tutorial chooses explicitly (docs/adr/0101)."
